VideoHaul is a media downloader that orchestrates external, independently
licensed engines. It does not bundle or redistribute them. Each managed engine
is installed once into a persistent per-user location, validated before reuse,
and downloaded again only when it is missing, broken, or incompatible.

The managed engines and browser runtime VideoHaul can install or reuse are listed
in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md together with their own licenses and project homepages.
Those components remain the property of their respective authors and are governed
by their own license terms, not by this project's license.

VideoHaul does not circumvent digital rights management, subscription controls,
authentication the user does not already possess, or any other access control.
The interactive Media Detector observes an ordinary browser session that the
user drives themselves; it neither decrypts protected media nor bypasses the
protections a site applies.

Users are responsible for ensuring that their use of VideoHaul complies with the
terms of service of the sites they access and with the copyright law of their
jurisdiction.
